  "_commit": {
    "id": "d0fbd4601dda6a4709c728fd51d78989c59ceaf0",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "fix: add missing sf-signature spatialMatch/spatialJoin methods (0.99.28)\n\nspatialMatch/spatialJoin had no method for a plain sf object. An sf is a\nbase S3 class (c(\"sf\", \"data.frame\")), not an S4Vectors::DataFrame, so\nthe existing DataFrame-signature methods never matched it -- calling\neither with a real sf object errored with \"unable to find an inherited\nmethod\" rather than falling through to anything.\n\nThis is purely a missing signature, not an S3/S4 dispatch limitation:\nsetMethod(generic, c(..., \"sf\"), ...) dispatches on the class vector\ndirectly, no setOldClass() bridging needed. Fixed by adding\nc(\"DuckDBDataFrame\", \"sf\") for spatialMatch, and both\nc(\"DuckDBDataFrame\", \"sf\")/c(\"sf\", \"DuckDBDataFrame\") for spatialJoin,\ndelegating to the same existing DuckDBSpatial calls (which already\nhandle sf input correctly as of DuckDBSpatial 0.99.8).\n\nAdded regression tests for all three new signatures. Full test suite:\n0 failures.\n",
    "time": 1792599210
  },
